---
bail()
---
Usage
-- `bail "CRASH REASON" "DEBUG INFORMATION"`
---- $1 is always output
---- if the user sets $DEBUG; $2 will be output as well
---- $3 is provided for custom exit code
---
Reason
-- bail() is used to provide a crash reason
---- via $1
-- and debug information
---- via $2
-- with custom exit code
---- via $3
---
Routine - as of v0.0.0.91
-- check if $DEBUG is set, this is automatically handled by ops() typically
  >> however users can manually export $DEBUG as well
---- if $DEBUG is unset then give crash reason and exit with code ${3:-1}
----- otherwise provide advanced debug info using $2, $orgfunc and $PWD
---
Legend
-- $orgfunc
---- $orgfunc is used for additional debug info
---- if set before bail() is called & DEBUG is set, output will contain info about last running function
---- calls serveral functions deep should have advanced info about pathways
  >> devs should append onto $orgfunc following existing formating clues
  >> when possible; it may be desirable to overwrite at times
-- $DEBUG
---- toggelled on by --verbose within ops() or can be manually exported
-- $PWD
---- provides the current path of rsh; always set by env
---
